templates/settings/settings.user.json:154:        "reason": "vigia PROTOCOL.md, que --ceremony user nao instala; advisory fail-OPEN sempre, entao o criterio antigo (bloqueia) era falso",
templates/settings/settings.user.json:231:        "_comment": "PLAN-124 WS-2 (ECC value-harvest) — adopter linter/formatter config protection, ADVISORY variant for the USER ceremony. Same hook as the maintainer ceremony but NON-BLOCKING: the top-level env sets CEO_CONFIG_PROTECTION_ADVISORY=1, so on an edit of an EXISTING adopter linter config the hook ALLOWS the tool call and attaches a systemMessage steer ('fix the code, not the config') instead of blocking. Per the user-ceremony doctrine this hook only ever reads/writes the adopter's own files and never blocks the session. Escape hatches still apply (CEO_CONFIG_PROTECTION=0 / <repo>/.claude/.config-protection-disable). To make it BLOCKING in a user install, remove CEO_CONFIG_PROTECTION_ADVISORY from env.",
templates/settings/settings.user.json:308:        "_comment": "PLAN-124 WS-2 (ECC value-harvest) — adopter linter/formatter config protection, ADVISORY variant for the USER ceremony. Same hook as the maintainer ceremony but NON-BLOCKING: the top-level env sets CEO_CONFIG_PROTECTION_ADVISORY=1, so on an edit of an EXISTING adopter linter config the hook ALLOWS the tool call and attaches a systemMessage steer ('fix the code, not the config') instead of blocking. Per the user-ceremony doctrine this hook only ever reads/writes the adopter's own files and never blocks the session. Escape hatches still apply (CEO_CONFIG_PROTECTION=0 / <repo>/.claude/.config-protection-disable). To make it BLOCKING in a user install, remove CEO_CONFIG_PROTECTION_ADVISORY from env.",
templates/settings/settings.user.json:320:        "_comment": "PLAN-190 W1: Workflow launch ledger + resume guard. Records script sha256 + snapshot, LITERAL args and code revision under <state-dir>/launches/ BEFORE dispatch; blocks a resumeFromRunId whose args differ from the strongly bound, validated manifest (script change: advisory unless CEO_WORKFLOW_SCRIPT_GUARD=enforce). Recovery: `ceo-launches.py relaunch <run>`. Override, recorded: a call description starting with 'CEO_WORKFLOW_RESUME_FORCE: <why>' or CEO_WORKFLOW_RESUME_FORCE=1; advisory CEO_WORKFLOW_RESUME_GUARD=0; off CEO_WORKFLOW_LEDGER=0. Fail-open on infrastructure.",
