templates/settings/settings.base.json:199:        "_comment": "PLAN-124 WS-2 (ECC value-harvest) — adopter linter/formatter config protection. BLOCKING (maintainer ceremony). Allows first-time CREATION of a config (ENOENT) but BLOCKS any Edit/Write/MultiEdit that MODIFIES an EXISTING file in the UNAMBIGUOUS adopter-linter basename allowlist (eslint/prettier/biome/ruff/stylelint/markdownlint/shellcheck/tslint/flake8 — NOT pyproject.toml/setup.cfg/package.json, NOT governance configs which are the canonical guard's job per MF-L/debate K6). The insight: an agent 'fixes' a failing lint gate by relaxing the config instead of the code → 'fix the code, not the config'. Design choice = block-any-edit (ECC parity, revisitable; see module docstring). Escape hatches: CEO_CONFIG_PROTECTION=0 (session) or <repo>/.claude/.config-protection-disable (per-repo). User ceremony wires the ADVISORY variant (CEO_CONFIG_PROTECTION_ADVISORY=1 → allow + systemMessage steer, never blocks). Fail-OPEN on a hook bug; fail-CLOSED (bounded) only on a write tool with no resolvable file path. Raw tool input is never echoed (basename + resolved path only). MIT-attributed re-implementation of ECC scripts/hooks/config-protection.js.",
templates/settings/settings.base.json:223:        "_comment": "PLAN-190 W1: Workflow launch ledger + resume guard. Records script sha256 + snapshot, LITERAL args and code revision under <state-dir>/launches/ BEFORE dispatch; blocks a resumeFromRunId whose args differ from the strongly bound, validated manifest (script change: advisory unless CEO_WORKFLOW_SCRIPT_GUARD=enforce). Recovery: `ceo-launches.py relaunch <run>`. Override, recorded: a call description starting with 'CEO_WORKFLOW_RESUME_FORCE: <why>' or CEO_WORKFLOW_RESUME_FORCE=1; advisory CEO_WORKFLOW_RESUME_GUARD=0; off CEO_WORKFLOW_LEDGER=0. Fail-open on infrastructure.",
