templates/settings/settings.base.json:459:        "_comment": "PLAN-179 W1-b [amendment r1-C3]: Constraint Pinning PRIMARY channel. On a post-compaction session start (matcher 'compact' — the hook ALSO re-checks source == 'compact' in-process, never trusting the matcher alone), re-states the pinned governance constraints from the CODE constant _lib/pinned_constraints.PINNED_CONSTRAINTS (r1-C5 — never read from a .md at runtime, so it cannot be evicted by the summarizer) via additionalContext. RULES, not pointers: the PostCompact reinject hook is the REINFORCEMENT channel, this is the primary one, so pinning does not depend on the still-open W0-1 PostCompact channel verdict. ADVISORY, fail-OPEN, never blocks; emits NO audit event (the action is not yet in _KNOWN_ACTIONS — registration is a follow-up ceremony). Kill-switch: CEO_CONSTRAINT_PINNING=0 (deliberately NOT the shared CEO_COMPACTION_CONTINUITY — PLAN-179 §8.8: turning off the continuity snapshot must not silently disarm the governance floor).",
templates/settings/settings.base.json:537:        "_comment": "PLAN-134 W1 #5 (E5-F2): closeout-guard — ADVISORY Stop reminder when the session did substantive work without a closeout (CLAUDE.md §Current Work + CHANGELOG + memory) and/or an Owner-GPG finish-*.sh ceremony is pending (staged/** or scripts/local/ newer than the last tag). Fail-OPEN, never blocks. Kill: CEO_CLOSEOUT_GUARD=0.",
templates/settings/settings.base.json:551:        "_comment": "PLAN-135 W2 H1 (ADR-153): PreCompact continuity snapshot — before the transcript collapses (manual /compact or auto context-window threshold), snapshots plan-id + execution-unit position + ceremony flags to the plan scratchpad + reads the HMAC-chain anchor. ADVISORY, fail-OPEN, never blocks. Emits closed-enum compaction_continuity_snapshot. Kill: CEO_COMPACTION_CONTINUITY=0.",
templates/settings/settings.base.json:642:  "_posture_keys_comment": "PLAN-163 T5.3/OQ5 — fail-closed posture keys (CC >=2.1.220). Key (1) permissions.defaultMode ships LIVE below (see _default_mode_arbitration_comment); the REMAINING keys ship COMMENTED for adopters. Dogfood status (2026-08-03): the framework repo enables workflowSizeGuideline and the sandbox keys; disableAutoMode was REMOVED from the dogfood settings by Owner decision (ceremony [SENT-PLAN165]) — beyond the documented no-mid-session-escalation effect it also strips 'auto' from the operator's native shift+tab mode cycle, and choosing the session mode is the operator's call, not the framework's. Adopters may still opt in. To adopt, add the keys literally: (2) top-level \"disableAutoMode\": \"disable\" — string enum whose sole value is 'disable' (the 2.1.220 schema rejects a boolean and SKIPS THE WHOLE settings file on mismatch — S286 live-fire); prevents automatic permission-mode escalation mid-session. (3) top-level \"workflowSizeGuideline\": <per your workflow scale; advisory sizing guideline for Workflow-tool fan-outs>. (4) \"sandbox\": { \"network\": { \"strictAllowlist\": true } } — tightens allowedDomains matching to the strict form. (5) \"sandbox\": { \"filesystem\": { \"disabled\": false } } — keeps filesystem confinement armed when the sandbox is enabled (true would fail-OPEN the FS layer). All keys are independent and additive; rollback is deleting the key. NEW-EVENT hook registrations (DirectoryAdded/Notification) are deliberately NOT in this template yet — T3.4 version-floor feature gate (upgrade.sh, default OFF), ADR-183 residual (e); this template stays at 45 registrations until the floor probe is recorded. This block is documentation only — underscore-prefixed keys are ignored by the harness.",
